--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PrivacyPage.tsx is a thin promotion wrapper: it sets a PageContainer (title,
subtitle, copyLink) and embeds <PrivacySection /> verbatim, so the browser-local
privacy controls — the "recently viewed pages" LRU clear (lib/recentPages) and
the tri-state cookie/GDPR consent control (lib/cookieConsent), plus the
deployment `require_cookie_consent` policy sentence (useVersionInfo) — live at
/account/privacy as a first-class Account route instead of buried in the dense
Settings page. The page itself declares no data of its own (the parity manifest
records zero dataSources, zero panels, and exactly two strings — requiredCount=2);
the embedded PrivacySection owns the recent-pages count + clear, the consent
tri-state (accept / decline / reset), the irreversible-clear confirmation dialog,
the version-policy feed, and the toast feedback.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 PrivacySection feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.privacy.PrivacySection, dir
apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/feature-views/PrivacySection/) and
owns every data state: the pre-resolution Loading skeleton, the resolved Content
body (recent-pages card + consent card), the version feed's stale/offline/error
freshness chrome (never a blanking gate), the clear-confirmation dialog, the four
mutations, and the toast queue — all unit-tested off-device by
PrivacySectionViewModelTest + PrivacyProjectionTest. It is fully self-wiring: the
composable resolves the on-device SharedPreferences recent-pages + cookie-consent
stores from LocalContext and the shared SettingsStore version policy from
LocalDataContainer, so the host passes nothing. This page is its host: it sets the
PageContainer-equivalent header and embeds the feature view — never
re-implementing it (DRY, ADR-006). Mirrors the sibling notifications/ChannelsPage
and notifications/WebhooksPage 2-string wrappers that embed shared feature views.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.settings.privacy):
  - PrivacyPageModel.kt   Registration(ROUTE_ID accountPrivacy,
                          WEB_PATH /account/privacy, SLUG PrivacyPage)
                          + recordPrivacyPageOpened (the one PII-safe view.opened
                          diagnostic, P1/S11). No page-level feed — the embedded
                          feature view owns the recent-pages/consent/version data.
  - PrivacyPage.kt        Stateful entry PrivacyPage(modifier, logger): records
                          view.opened, then PrivacyPageContent (verticalScroll
                          Column: header + PrivacySection()) + PrivacyPageHeader
                          (PageTitle + subtitle BodyText + copy-link IconButton
                          writing WEB_PATH to the clipboard).
  - PrivacyPageHost.kt    PrivacyRoute() renders PrivacyPage(); PrivacyPageHost
                          .register() -> PageHosts.register("accountPrivacy").
                          Idempotent.

Edits (registration + string catalog + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt  import + PrivacyPageHost.register() at process start
                             (after WebhooksPageHost.register()). The accountPrivacy
                             /account/privacy destination already exists in
                             Destinations.kt (NavGroup.Settings) — host wiring only.
  - res/values/strings.xml (+ values-ar, values-he)  2 generated keys
                             translation_account_privacy_{title,subtitle} inserted
                             in sorted position (before translation_addressInput_label),
                             generator-identical format (no tokens, no chars needing
                             escaping); ar/he carry the English fallback (placeholder
                             locales, translated=false). copy-link reuses the existing
                             translation_common_copyLink_action.
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:settings/Privacy row (done, 2/2).

Notes:
  - i18n catalog: res/values*/strings.xml is AUTO-GENERATED by
    apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts. The web page sources
    account.privacy.{title,subtitle} as inline t() fallback defaults (they are not
    yet in the canonical i18n catalog source, which is outside this artifact's
    allowed files: com/teslasync/settings/**, NavHost registration,
    res/values*/strings.xml, this log). The two keys were hand-inserted into the
    three Android strings.xml files byte-identically to the generator output
    (sorted between activity_viewAll <-> addressInput_label; no escapable chars),
    so a future gen-i18n run — once the keys are added to the catalog source —
    re-emits these exact lines (no conflict). No gen-i18n step runs in the gradle
    gate, so the committed strings.xml is authoritative for the build. Honest
    disclosure (no silent drift, covenant #9).
  - SI: no field on this surface is unit-bearing — no SI conversion (ADR-013 n/a).
  - States: PrivacySection renders Loading skeleton / Content (recent + consent
    cards) / version stale-offline / version error+retry — verified by the shared
    PrivacySectionViewModelTest. A missing version response falls back to
    requireConsent=false and never blanks the panel (web parity).
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading + copy-link IconButton contentDescription; the feature
    view supplies the shield IconBox + card content + dynamic/dark theme (ADR-015).
  - Layout: PrivacySection lays out as a non-lazy GlassPanel Column, so it composes
    safely inside the page's outer verticalScroll container.

